                        libros ethicorum et qui alienaverit anathema sit. Amen’ (fol. 1v)‘(This [the
                        inscription on fol. 1v] appears to be in a 14th-cent. hand; if so, the
                        College must have owned and lost the volume before it was acquired by Rook.)
                        Below this, an erasure seemingly of an inventory-mark: 89 (?) textus.’
                        (Mynors, Balliol, 294)</p></provenance>
